{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Immersive Theme Doc Sync",
  "description": "Whenever any immersive feature file changes, update IMMERSIVE-STORE.md to keep the theme doc accurate — file structure, architecture, settings tables, and locale keys.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "layout/theme.liquid",
      "templates/index.json",
      "sections/immersive-canvas.liquid",
      "sections/glass-panel.liquid",
      "sections/glass-product.liquid",
      "sections/immersive-product-grid.liquid",
      "snippets/immersive-product-card.liquid",
      "snippets/virtual-tryon.liquid",
      "assets/immersive-store.js",
      "assets/immersive-theme.css",
      "locales/en.default.json",
      "locales/en.default.schema.json"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "An immersive theme file was just edited. Re-read IMMERSIVE-STORE.md and update it as needed:\n\n1. File Structure section — if files were added, removed, or repurposed\n2. Architecture subsections — if behavior of immersive-store.js, immersive-canvas.liquid, Section Rendering API usage, room configuration, or session state changed\n3. Any tables (room settings, product panel settings, product grid settings, locale keys) — keep them in sync with current schemas and translation keys in the code\n\nKeep the doc accurate to the current implementation, high-level and readable for future devs — not just a dump of schema JSON.\n\nIf a change is too large to summarize confidently, add a short \"TODO: verify docs for X\" note with a link to the changed file and section.\n\nOnly update what actually changed — do not rewrite sections that are still accurate."
  }
}